#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee8953ef-d003-5c9b-88a8-5468ca45d955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371974} {:answer/id #uuid "f37572b7-9528-52c2-a5d2-02d7f4edcfba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371975} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9ef6b1-c99c-58a9-9777-128812eef6dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371976} {:answer/id #uuid "ebcbdacd-d15e-5554-a4fc-50a72a6e9bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371977} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6c01be-2aac-5727-9be5-288fcf6f2dfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f6c01be-2aac-5727-9be5-288fcf6f2dfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371978} :answer-field/id #uuid "abaee53d-d46f-5943-bf04-854bdddfdac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53682f47-d6df-5316-a70a-740ac7546bd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161683" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xz$-plane and the surface $y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=3,$ $z=0,$ $z=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[y]_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]}_{z=0}^{z=\\pi }\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}-{x}^{2}(-1-1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({3}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d26231b-a433-5443-9a66-120f82a6997c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371981} {:answer/id #uuid "46717e8d-a243-51c9-98d9-706d9dde52cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371982} {:answer/id #uuid "98fc5a07-76ba-57d6-afc7-438784aa6eaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371983} {:answer/id #uuid "f93d0e70-c408-55b5-a8dc-3cf5737c3a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371984} {:answer/id #uuid "da393ccb-4d50-5119-879a-52d5b43446ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f93d0e70-c408-55b5-a8dc-3cf5737c3a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371984} :answer-field/id #uuid "782c3ae4-8b27-54ba-966c-75d8bf24c907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bfe9041-7839-5cd8-91c3-2fefd82606bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161696" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/cf19d77966b23604f18c4194b4166536ff2f12267cbc55a98a436bda9fc3c098.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/a7261baec0c907779f5b1f5ff669ca826d4b93c5dd1b9a389e0989fe34756a6e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-2y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/65c61ad7dc2964cd0de9a6bbdf259fcf3388e25da4eaabf155d58ff0c05c8d55.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-2y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-2y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-x-2y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4-x-2y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[(4-x)y-{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-1\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(6-2)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e3adb0-600c-59cf-a5ec-3e48ce3ab32c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371988} {:answer/id #uuid "c88cecee-b7ec-516e-b590-0208ea994ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371989} {:answer/id #uuid "3d2f278e-3a1a-5fde-9bcf-1433fee8770b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371990} {:answer/id #uuid "54f1e135-bb40-5e6e-946f-e83618bccc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371991} {:answer/id #uuid "5453f0c0-51bc-5ea4-ab19-36405353bc53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15+{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54f1e135-bb40-5e6e-946f-e83618bccc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371991} :answer-field/id #uuid "13a40faf-0664-59a8-bc58-82602a9c7ea9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5673a864-be41-56e2-8c5e-6dd4bdd6d6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161704" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $z=3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{5}}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}^{3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-(-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\sqrt{5}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{5}}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}}}\\,5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(5-{x}^{2})+(5-{x}^{2})+(5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216feacc-e9c7-5af7-af2c-3beac6ebf67d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371995} {:answer/id #uuid "5a45cdf1-c4ca-5f90-879a-ec2f9695567b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371996} {:answer/id #uuid "51e3e831-8913-52d6-981c-b5e7dc25b552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371997} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4d6dd2-b9f4-532b-974a-991cd7b7bda5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371998} {:answer/id #uuid "6b445c74-3cb8-50dd-9a74-9c084012b303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "216feacc-e9c7-5af7-af2c-3beac6ebf67d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371995} :answer-field/id #uuid "3719ef16-1188-51e3-9e14-c1f83e5a66eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "644598bd-1b73-5a33-88b9-41dbd3e91715" :question/math-academy-id "q-163118" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/33d603d41e211e402165a33c98eb01965b3f49358999d0223ea320c6197525a0.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/2a71dcc574b324a0904b21edf1559f80d1ffe0e35ab0b0fd5cec8b31317ec548.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y+2z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/c0bb526b2e56649ebadf7a3989340858451356e24fa205a0f3b26579f22315a2.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y+2z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+2z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}y+2z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[yz+{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(y(2)+{2}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2y+4\\,dy \\\\  & =[{y}^{2}+4y]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =({2}^{2}+4(2))-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55b693ef-68a3-5d58-9946-2c0a5a7385ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-6{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372002} {:answer/id #uuid "13fb5c1e-5f54-5b01-96b3-a4556c82db02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372003} {:answer/id #uuid "dd666482-b6fe-55bd-82d3-ff33b5522b7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372004} {:answer/id #uuid "26f86163-56d6-5dba-9c93-1951236ce0f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-8{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372005} {:answer/id #uuid "083fd3fb-33f9-5f61-ad77-415b3753b957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "083fd3fb-33f9-5f61-ad77-415b3753b957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372006} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa390be2-1699-54e9-aff9-cdb2c797c0c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8beb19b-c712-51be-adb7-7e5863ff49db" :question/math-academy-id "q-163221" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ and $z=3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}^{3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})-(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})+(1-2{x}^{2})+(2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
